"We Thought We Were Fucked, But..."

A Citizenship 9 Lesson on Perception vs Reality

---

The Point (Sharpened)

When predictions of disaster don't come true, people stop believing warnings — even when the warnings are real.

This makes it harder to:
- Take climate change seriously
- Evaluate immigration claims
- Assess whether the world is getting better or worse
- Make informed voting decisions

The skill: Learn to separate evidence from emotion when evaluating risk claims.

