Teacher Notes

Common student pushback:
- "But climate change IS real and serious" — YES. That's exactly why you need to understand the cry-wolf problem. Real risks get dismissed because of fake ones.
- "Some things ARE getting worse" — YES. Compare to actual data. Don't assume either way.
- "I don't trust statistics" — Good instinct. But then verify, not dismiss.

The goal isn't cynicism. It's calibrated trust — knowing when to be scared, when to push back, and when to look up the numbers.

Core message: The world is neither falling apart nor achieving utopia. Both sides have an incentive to exaggerate. Your job is to find the actual data.

